---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: sprints-dir-governance
purpose: "Auto-generated sprint results + journals — born without lifecycle frontmatter. Advise, never block, so the shift tooling is not gated by the parent deny."
rules:
  - id: doc-frontmatter-at-birth
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    require-frontmatter: [id]
    why: "Sprint results are auto-generated; ideally carry an `id` for citation, but creation here is never blocked."
---
# sprints — auto-generated shift output

Sprint results and journals are generated by the shift skill as markdown-heading output, not
authored design docs. The parent `superpowers/.epr-meta` deny (`require-frontmatter: [id, status,
cites]`) would hard-block them; this child overrides that rule (same `id`, nearest-wins) with a
non-blocking `inject`, so generation is never gated. Edits to existing results are untouched.
